      <activity id="aa1d5440-b597-586b-a72a-be928b3660a9" activityNameId="c2e64156-0564-5628-933c-571600aefa6a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Steel board, 20 mm, powder coated, cardboard filled, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Steel board, 20 mm, powder coated, cardboard filled, at plant
na;
UUID: b354edc2-0dae-33ca-9f08-1bc3fe9232d3
This data set includes the materials and resources needed for producing steel kitchen front panels per m2. The panel has a mounting plate of corrugated cardboard which is coverd with the steel sheets and pressed. The cardboard core is  2 cm wide and used for front covers. It is assumed that the pressing consumes as much electricity as the steel processing of Franke (kitchen worktop production). Transport is estimated according to the ecoinvent standard distances for Switzerland.; Geography: Data valid for Switzerland
Location:  Data valid for Switzerland
Technology: Average processes for producing steel kitchen panels.
Time period: &lt;null&gt;
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b354edc2-0dae-33ca-9f08-1bc3fe9232d3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
